    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "obtained from these incidences of feudalism by large payments to the Crown inreturn forcharters covenanting that Malta should for ever be administered under the royal exchequer without the intervention of intermediary feudal lords. This compact was twice broken, and in 1428 the Maltese paid King Alfonso 30,000 florins for a confirmation of privileges, with a proviso that entitled them to resist by force of arms any intermediate lord that his successors might attempt to impose. Under the Aragonese, Malta, as regards localaffairs, was administered bya Universita or"
  }, {
